                <pb facs="0711" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.24/159: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-25T12:00:00-06:00">April 25,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>73. Honduran Government has ordered 450,000 cartridges for army rifles from the
                    Remington Arms Company to be shipped from New York to Tela consigned Minister of
                    War Government Honduras.</p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s instruction No. 117, March 20, license for export
                    should be approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
